PEAT now writes a self-contained HTML report (``peat-report.html``) to the run directory at the end of ``scan``, ``pull``, ``push``, ``parse``, ``pillage`` and ``heat`` runs, summarizing the run, the hosts and devices found, per-device details and saved files (with SHA-256 hashes), warnings and errors, and the configuration. The report works offline, escapes all device data, and uses a strict Content Security Policy. It can be disabled with ``--no-html-report`` or ``html_report: false``, and regenerated for existing run directories with the new ``peat report`` command, which treats run directories as untrusted (it never reads files outside of them or writes through symlinks).
